# React Component Patterns

## Component Structure
- All components are functional React 18 components in TypeScript JSX
- Prefer **Pure UI**: components in `_contents` and `components/` accept data via props
- No data-fetching logic in presentational components
- Pass `className` through `cn()` helper for conditional classes

## Import Convention
Always import from shared UI library or folder barrels – never deep-link files:

```ts
// ✅ Correct - Shared UI Components
import { Card, PageWrapper, Dialog } from "@repo/multiverse-ui";
import { Badge, Table, Avatar } from "@repo/multiverse-ui";
import { Button, FormInput, DatePicker } from "@repo/multiverse-ui";

// ✅ Correct - App-specific Components
import { LoginForm, UserForm } from "app/login/_contents";
import { useLoginMutation } from "app/login/_hooks";

// ❌ Incorrect
import Card from "@repo/multiverse-ui/src/components/containers/Card";
```

## Component Categories
From `@repo/multiverse-ui`:
- `containers/`: Layout wrappers, page chrome, dialogs, cards, modals
- `informationals/`: Pure display (badges, stats, tables, avatars, tooltips)
- `input_controls/`: Form inputs & controls (buttons, inputs, selectors, date pickers)
- `navigationals/`: Navigation widgets (tabs, pagination, breadcrumbs, sidebar)

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid arbitrary values unless design tokens unavailable
- CSS-in-JS not used; colocated `.css` files for complex selectors
- Component-specific styles go in sibling `.css` file when inline length excessive

